{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.YLambdaRecipeNormaliser","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.YLambdaRecipeNormaliser","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WenzlNormalisation"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.wenzlWeight_eq_recipe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.wenzlWeight_eq_recipe","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YLambdaRecipeNormaliser.lean#L97-L109","doc":"**The recipe's output is `wenzlWeight`.**\n\n`y_λ = s_λ / Z_n` — step 4 of the recipe — is `wenzlWeight r Q λ`, once `Z_n` is\nthe closed form above.  So the `y_lambda` field of `QOU.Hecke.WedderburnDecomp`,\nwhose docstring gives precisely this recipe, has a proved closed form on the\nWenzl lattice rather than only a prose one.\n\nStated per-diagram; `hν` is what ties the recipe's `n` to the diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dim_schurPrincipal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dim_schurPrincipal","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YLambdaRecipeNormaliser.lean#L69-L95","doc":"**The recipe's `Z_n`, in closed form.**\n\n`∑_{μ ⊢ n} f^μ · s_μ(1, Q, …, Q^{r−1}) = [r]_Q ^ n`.\n\nStep 4 of `prop:y-lambda-recipe-from-partition` sums over every partition of `n`\nto build its normaliser; on the Wenzl lattice that sum is `[r]_Q ^ n`.\n\nThis is `sum_dim_wenzlWeight_eq_one` with the normalisation cleared: the weight\ndivides by `[r]_Q ^ |μ|` per diagram, and every diagram in the sum has `|μ| = n`,\nso the whole sum scales by the single factor `[r]_Q ^ n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}